{
  "id": "dm_cisco_ios_config_change_snmp_trap",
  "conf": {
    "output": "default",
    "description": "Cisco IOS/IOS-XE config-change / snmp-trap: no stock branch parses CONFIG_I, CFGLOG_LOGGEDCMD, RELOAD, RESTART or LOGGINGHOST_STARTSTOP, so this is a genuine Cribl-side reparse of clogHistMsgText for the change-control/anti-tamper family, per direct.elastic recommendation.",
    "functions": [
      {
        "id": "comment",
        "filter": "true",
        "conf": {
          "comment": "cisco-ios / config-change / snmp-trap. Upstream SNMP trap receiver decodes the PDU and forwards varbinds as JSON in _raw. Dissects CONFIG_I ('Configured from X by Y'), CFGLOG_LOGGEDCMD ('User:U logged command:C', tolerant of the one-vs-two-space variant before 'logged command:' the brief calls out), RELOAD, RESTART and LOGGINGHOST_STARTSTOP bodies. event.action is derived from event.code (clogHistMsgName) by lookup since no message in this family carries an action token, per recommendation. No masking is applied to CFGLOG_LOGGEDCMD command text: the map's masking/length-cap guidance for logged commands is guarded-route-specific ('cap that field's length before anything leaves the enclave') and direct.elastic explicitly says to retain full command lines for this route -- documented decision, not an oversight."
        },
        "description": "document the varbind source, which mnemonic bodies are reparsed, and why no masking is applied on the direct route"
      },
      {
        "id": "serde",
        "filter": "true",
        "conf": {
          "mode": "extract",
          "type": "json",
          "srcField": "_raw"
        },
        "description": "extract the JSON-encoded varbind object the upstream SNMP trap receiver forwards"
      },
      {
        "id": "regex_extract",
        "filter": "clogHistMsgName === 'CONFIG_I' || clogHistMsgName === 'CONFIG' || clogHistMsgName === 'CONFIG_NV_I'",
        "conf": {
          "regex": "/Configured from (?<cfg_source>\\S+) by (?<cfg_user>\\S+)(?:\\s+on\\s+(?<cfg_line>.+))?$/",
          "source": "clogHistMsgText"
        },
        "description": "dissect the CONFIG_I/CONFIG/CONFIG_NV_I config-source-and-actor grammar"
      },
      {
        "id": "regex_extract",
        "filter": "clogHistMsgName === 'CFGLOG_LOGGEDCMD'",
        "conf": {
          "regex": "/User:(?<cfg_cmd_user>\\S+)\\s+logged command:(?<cfg_command>.+)$/",
          "source": "clogHistMsgText"
        },
        "description": "dissect the per-command CFGLOG_LOGGEDCMD grammar, tolerant of one or two spaces before 'logged command:'"
      },
      {
        "id": "regex_extract",
        "filter": "clogHistMsgName === 'RELOAD'",
        "conf": {
          "regex": "/Reload requested by (?<reload_user>[^.]+)\\.\\s*Reload [Rr]eason:\\s*(?<reload_reason>.+)$/",
          "source": "clogHistMsgText"
        },
        "description": "dissect the RELOAD requester and reason"
      },
      {
        "id": "regex_extract",
        "filter": "clogHistMsgName === 'RESTART'",
        "conf": {
          "regex": "/System restarted -- (?<restart_banner>.+)$/",
          "source": "clogHistMsgText"
        },
        "description": "dissect the RESTART version banner"
      },
      {
        "id": "regex_extract",
        "filter": "clogHistMsgName === 'LOGGINGHOST_STARTSTOP'",
        "conf": {
          "regex": "/Logging to host (?<log_host_ip>\\S+) port (?<log_host_port>\\d+)\\s+(?<log_host_state>started|stopped)/",
          "source": "clogHistMsgText"
        },
        "description": "dissect the LOGGINGHOST_STARTSTOP collector address/port/state -- 'stopped' is the device announcing it is about to go dark"
      },
      {
        "id": "eval",
        "filter": "true",
        "conf": {
          "add": [
            {
              "name": "event.category",
              "value": "['configuration']"
            },
            {
              "name": "user.name",
              "value": "__e['cfg_user'] || __e['cfg_cmd_user'] || __e['reload_user']"
            },
            {
              "name": "cisco.ios.config.source",
              "value": "__e['cfg_source']"
            },
            {
              "name": "cisco.ios.config.line",
              "value": "__e['cfg_line']"
            },
            {
              "name": "process.command_line",
              "value": "__e['cfg_command']"
            },
            {
              "name": "cisco.ios.reload.reason",
              "value": "__e['reload_reason']"
            },
            {
              "name": "cisco.ios.restart.banner",
              "value": "__e['restart_banner']"
            },
            {
              "name": "cisco.ios.logging_host.ip",
              "value": "__e['log_host_ip']"
            },
            {
              "name": "cisco.ios.logging_host.port",
              "value": "__e['log_host_port'] !== undefined ? Number(__e['log_host_port']) : undefined"
            },
            {
              "name": "event.action",
              "value": "(__e['clogHistMsgName'] === 'CONFIG_I' || __e['clogHistMsgName'] === 'CONFIG' || __e['clogHistMsgName'] === 'CONFIG_NV_I') ? 'config-change' : (__e['clogHistMsgName'] === 'CFGLOG_LOGGEDCMD' ? 'command-executed' : (__e['clogHistMsgName'] === 'RELOAD' ? 'reload-requested' : (__e['clogHistMsgName'] === 'RESTART' ? 'system-restarted' : (__e['clogHistMsgName'] === 'LOGGINGHOST_STARTSTOP' ? (__e['log_host_state'] === 'started' ? 'logging-started' : (__e['log_host_state'] === 'stopped' ? 'logging-stopped' : undefined)) : undefined))))"
            },
            {
              "name": "event.severity",
              "value": "__e['clogHistSeverity'] !== undefined ? Number(__e['clogHistSeverity']) - 1 : undefined"
            },
            {
              "name": "log.level",
              "value": "__e['clogHistSeverity'] !== undefined ? ['emergency','alert','critical','error','warning','notice','informational','debug'][Number(__e['clogHistSeverity']) - 1] : undefined"
            },
            {
              "name": "cisco.ios.snmp.sysuptime",
              "value": "__e['clogHistTimestamp']"
            },
            {
              "name": "cisco.ios.snmp.history_index",
              "value": "__e['clogHistIndex']"
            },
            {
              "name": "cisco.ios.snmp.truncated",
              "value": "__e['clogHistMsgText'] ? __e['clogHistMsgText'].length >= 254 : undefined"
            }
          ],
          "remove": [
            "cfg_source",
            "cfg_user",
            "cfg_line",
            "cfg_cmd_user",
            "cfg_command",
            "reload_user",
            "reload_reason",
            "restart_banner",
            "log_host_ip",
            "log_host_port",
            "log_host_state",
            "clogHistSeverity",
            "clogHistTimestamp",
            "clogHistIndex"
          ]
        },
        "description": "per direct.elastic: derive event.action from event.code by lookup (no message in this family carries an action token), extract account/line/source/command per branch, keep event.category=configuration even though the command lands in process.command_line, and convert the inverted MIB severity via the shared lookup"
      },
      {
        "id": "rename",
        "filter": "true",
        "conf": {
          "rename": [
            {
              "currentName": "clogHistMsgText",
              "newName": "event.original"
            },
            {
              "currentName": "clogHistMsgName",
              "newName": "event.code"
            },
            {
              "currentName": "clogHistFacility",
              "newName": "cisco.ios.facility"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "map the straight 1:1 CISCO-SYSLOG-MIB varbinds onto their ECS/custom targets (event.original was already reparsed above)"
      },
      {
        "id": "eval",
        "filter": "true",
        "conf": {
          "add": [
            {
              "name": "event.dataset",
              "value": "'cisco_ios.config_change'"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "tag the event with its dataset"
      }
    ]
  }
}
